  "live_records": {
    "q-96778": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96778",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given that $X∼U\\{3,7,9,10\\},$ compute $P(X=9).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{3,7,9,10\\},$ and the set $S=\\{3,7,9,10\\}$ has $|S|=4$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}, & x=3,7,9,10 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=9)=f(9)=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
