    "q-96810": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96810",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given $X∼U\\{9,10,11,…,17\\},$ compute $P(X<12).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{9,10,11,…,17\\},$ and the set $S=\\{9,10,11,…,17\\}$ has $|S|=17-9+1=9$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9}, & x=9,10,11,…,17 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ the items that satisfy $X<12$ are $9,10,11.$ There are $3$ of these items. Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(X<12)=3\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
