    "q-164160": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164160",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Given $X∼U\\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\},$ compute $P(X<2).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\},$ and the set $S=\\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\}$ has $|S|=6$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}, & x=0,1,2,3,4,5 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ there are $2$ items $(0,1)$ that satisfy $X<2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(X<2)=2\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-164160-a",
