    "q-96838": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96838",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given $X∼U\\{11,13,14,16,20\\},$ compute $P(13\\le X<16).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{11,13,14,16,20\\},$ and the set $S=\\{11,13,14,16,20\\}$ has $|S|=5$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}, & x=11,13,14,16,20 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ there are $2$ items $(13,14)$ that satisfies $13\\le X<16.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(13\\le X<16)=2\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
