    "q-96839": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96839",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Given $X∼U\\{1,2,3,…,17\\},$ compute $P(2\\le X<9).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{1,2,3,…,17\\},$ and the set $S=\\{1,2,3,…,17\\}$ has $|S|=17-1+1=17$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{17}, & x=1,2,3,…,17 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ there are $7$ items $(2,3,4,5,6,7,8)$ that satisfy $2\\le X<9.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(2\\le X<9)=7\\cdot \\frac{1}{17}=\\frac{7}{17}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-96839-a",
